# The Masamune: "If a creature dying causes a triggered ability of this creature or an emblem you own to trigger, that ability
# triggers an additional time" (CR 603.2d, 114.4). Sephiroth's emblem, "Whenever a creature dies, target opponent loses 1 life
# and you gain 1 life", is Bot1's (see the Sephiroth scenario for how it comes: four deaths on turn 3, 20 - 4 = 16 and 24).
# Turn 5: Bot1 casts The Masamune and equips Sephiroth, One-Winged Angel, who attacks sacrificing the Ornithopter: the death
# triggers the emblem twice, 14 and 26, then the Angel's 5 damage: Bot2 ends at 9. Without The Masamune it would be 15 and 25.

